cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite both the software itself and the paper
  that describes the classification it implements.
title: MMGenomicClassification
abstract: >-
  Reference implementation of the genomic classification of multiple myeloma into
  eleven groups from copy number, driver mutations, translocations and mutational
  signatures. Supports hg19, hg38 and mm10.
type: software
license: MIT
authors:
  - family-names: Ziccheddu
    given-names: Bachisio
repository-code: "https://github.com/OWNER/MMGenomicClassification"
keywords:
  - multiple myeloma
  - genomic classification
  - copy number
  - mutational signatures
  - bioinformatics
references:
  - type: article
    scope: >-
      Cite this paper when reporting results produced with this software.
    authors:
      - family-names: Maura
        given-names: Francesco
      - family-names: Rustad
        given-names: Even H
      - family-names: Boyle
        given-names: Eileen M
    title: >-
      Genomic Classification and Individualized Prognosis in Multiple Myeloma
    journal: Journal of Clinical Oncology
    doi: 10.1200/JCO.23.01277
